  "summaries": {
    "en": "Turf ink routing, weapon role assignments, and ranked-mode map control strategies for competitive Splatoon 3.",
    "ja": "チョウチンアンコウやターフ塗りルーティング、武器役割分担、ランクマッチのマップコントロール戦略を解説するスプラトゥーン3攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "shooter",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541701494587-cb58502866ab?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Painting turf underneath your own feet while moving is the single most impactful movement habit—it provides constant escape routes, refills ink faster, and forces opponents to commit to entering your paint.",
      "Each weapon class fills a distinct role: Shooters frontline, Chargers hold high ground, Rollers ambush and zone, Blasters area-deny. Run teams with at least two different class roles to avoid single-counter compositions.",
      "Special weapons dictate round tempo—activate Specials to contest point objectives, not as panic buttons. Use Trizooka or Booyah Bomb when the enemy has overextended into your turf, not when you are retreating.",
      "The Super Jump animation is telegraphed 1 second before landing—never Super Jump to a teammate under pressure; wait for the opponent to reposition before jumping to contested areas.",
      "In Ranked Splat Zones, your team's zone-control time stacks only when you fully paint the zone; a single unpainted tile stops accumulation. Prioritise complete zone coverage over eliminations when contesting."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "移動中に自分の足元を塗り続けることが最も影響の大きい習慣。逃げルートを常に確保し、インク回復を加速させ、相手に自分のエリアへの侵入コストを払わせる。",
      "武器クラスごとの役割を明確にする。シューターは前衛、チャージャーは高台確保、ローラーは奇襲とゾーン管理、ブラスターはエリア拒否。単一クラス構成は1つの対策で崩される。",
      "スペシャル武器はラウンドのテンポを決める。逃げる時ではなく、相手が自陣に踏み込んだ好機に発動する。トリプルトルネードやバリアをパニックで使わない。",
      "スーパージャンプは着地1秒前からアニメーションが見える。プレッシャー下の味方にスーパージャンプしない。相手が動いた後に安全な地点にジャンプする。",
      "ガチエリアでは、ゾーン全体を完全に塗った時のみカウントが進む。1マスの未塗りがカウントを止める。撃破よりゾーン完全塗装を優先する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Turf War Ink Routing",
        "body": "In Turf War, the first 30 seconds determine map-side control for the rest of the match. Route your ink path to claim the center line immediately, then split to cover flanks. Never start by painting your own spawn area exclusively—this concedes center turf at the opening bell, which takes 90+ seconds to reclaim. Assign one player to go wide on the right flank while three push center; the wide player applies pressure that forces opponents to split their ink coverage."
      },
      {
        "title": "Weapon Matchup Awareness",
        "body": "Learn the effective range of your weapon class against the most common counter-weapons (Chargers counter Shooters at long range; Rollers counter Chargers at close range). When you identify a hard counter in the enemy team, use terrain to negate the range advantage: cut off sightlines with walls and play around corners to stay out of the counter-weapon's optimal zone. In ranked modes, the first 20 seconds should be spent identifying enemy weapon types before committing to a role position."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Ranked Mode: Rainmaker Carries",
        "body": "The Rainmaker carrier should never move without at least two teammates painting the path ahead. The carrier's movement speed is reduced 40% compared to baseline—ink the path at least 5 tiles ahead of the carrier at all times. When the carrier is forced to stop, the shield-bearer role rotates to the nearest teammate. Most Rainmaker losses come from the carrier moving into enemy paint without a painted escape route; prioritise route creation over point advancement speed."
      },
      {
        "title": "Tower Control Timing",
        "body": "In Tower Control, the tower moves at full speed only when at least one player is on it and no opponents are contesting. Stagger your approach: one player rides first and draws fire while others flank. When the tower is near the enemy goal, two players should be on the tower simultaneously to survive the burst of Special weapons that enemies throw at checkpoint pushes. Do not use your own Special while riding—dismount, activate Special, then reboard."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Clam Blitz Clam Economy",
        "body": "In Clam Blitz, collect 10 clams to form a Power Clam before approaching the enemy basket—throwing individual clams is lower value than a Power Clam throw. The Power Clam opens the enemy basket for 15 seconds; ensure 2+ teammates are nearby before throwing. The most effective Clam Blitz cycle is: collect Power Clam → basket open → mass-deposit regular clams → retreat and recollect. Wasting a Power Clam throw with no follow-up clam deposits is the most common losing pattern."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Ignoring your own ink refill—out-of-ink in open terrain is nearly always lethal; squid-swim into your own turf before ink drops below 30%.",
      "Suiciding for eliminations in Ranked modes—in objective modes, deaths cost 5–10 seconds of objective time; only push for eliminations when the opponent is near your basket/zone.",
      "Activating Special weapons when already winning a zone—Specials are more valuable when reclaiming lost objectives than extending comfortable leads.",
      "Jumping predictably in combat—Jump attacks are common, but jumping in the same pattern twice gives opponents free aim time; mix landing positions.",
      "Not tracking enemy Special weapon meters on the HUD—the enemy Special meter is visible in ranked; anticipate Special activations before they happen rather than reacting after."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "インク残量の管理を怠る。開けた地形でインク切れはほぼ即死。インクが30%を下回る前に自陣に潜って回復する。",
      "ランクマッチで撃破のために突撃して死亡する。オブジェクトモードでの死亡はオブジェクト進行時間5〜10秒の損失。相手がバスケット/エリア近くにいる時のみ積極的に狙う。",
      "エリアを制圧している時にスペシャルを使う。スペシャルは有利状況の拡大より、失ったオブジェクトを取り返す時の方が価値が高い。",
      "戦闘中に予測可能なジャンプを繰り返す。ジャンプ攻撃は一般的だが、同じパターンを2回繰り返すと相手に狙い目を与える。着地位置を変える。",
      "HUD上の敵スペシャルゲージを確認しない。ランクマッチでは敵のスペシャルゲージが見える。発動後に反応するのではなく、発動前に予測して動く。"
    ]
  },
